COMIC#DEN#SHOOT
RIOT#DOVES#DUDE
ALP#FORESTS#TEN
N##TO#ANT#NO##D
KISSES#I#SABERS
#TEAS#ONE#POLE#
DEAR#EAGLE#EASY
AMI#IRK#EAR#TIY
BIDS#REACT#STAY
#ZONE#NUT#BAIT#
BELOVE#D#DANCED
R##WE#AIL#BE##A
APE#RAGTIME#FOR
VERA#NEEDS#SALT
ENEMY#DDS#WORDS


A1. A popular kind of Valentine when we were kids. ~ COMIC
A5. A married man's sanctum-sanctorum. ~ DEN
A8. Something African golfers do. ~ SHOOT
A13. A debate between the K. K. K. and Knights of Columbus. ~ RIOT
A14. Love birds. ~ DOVES
A16. The kind of a fellow who likes spats. ~ DUDE
A17. A difficult thing for a Swiss yodler to get over. ~ ALP
A18. Places with a shady reputation. ~ FORESTS
A20. Large Richard. (You'll have to ask an exponent of the ivory cubes for this one.) ~ TEN
A21. Preposition. ~ TO
A22. This would crawl a mile for a picnic. ~ ANT
A23. A very difficult word to say. ~ NO
A25. These are nothings divided by two. ~ KISSES
A28. Cavalry arms. ~ SABERS
A31. Afternoon cat fights. ~ TEAS
A32. A lonely number. ~ ONE
A34. When a man of this nationality gets married he should have a wooden wedding. ~ POLE
A35. "Talk is cheap," but this is expensive. ~ DEAR
A36. This bird is king of them all. ~ EAGLE
A38. Get this one; it's not hard. ~ EASY
A40. A friend in France. ~ AMI
A41. This rhymes with "work" and means to trouble. ~ IRK
A42. A sound organ. ~ EAR
A43. A pen that can't be used to write with. ~ TIY
A44. Entreats, proposes, offers or commands. ~ BIDS
A46. What rattlesnakes do when they're molested. ~ REACT
A48. What guests do when you want to go to bed. ~ STAY
A49. A division—we used to live in a temperate one, but not since prohibition. ~ ZONE
A51. The one that holds the steering wheel is the cause of most automobile accidents. ~ NUT
A52. What girls use make-up for. ~ BAIT
A53. To regard with affection. ~ BELOVE
A54. What Salome did to get a head. ~ DANCED
A56. This includes all of us. ~ WE
A57. Indisposition. (There's a Krazy Krack word for you!) ~ AIL
A59. To have existence. ~ BE
A60. Something society ladies do to keep in the social whirl. ~ APE
A63. The ancestor of Jazz. ~ RAGTIME
A66. In favor of. ~ FOR
A68. A girl's name. ~ VERA
A70. Necessities. ~ NEEDS
A71. A seasonable subject. ~ SALT
A72. A foe of the Swedish navy. ~ ENEMY
A73. This man holds his job through pull. (A degree.) ~ DDS
A74. The missiles thrown in a feminine fight. ~ WORDS

D1. An optimist is a person who takes this off his flivver. ~ CRANK
D2. A synonym for scandal in Washington. ~ OIL
D3. Something people use to remove wet spots. ~ MOP
D4. A pronoun. ~ IT
D5. That dumb girl. ~ DORA
D6. In lover's chronology—when the heavenly sessions begin. ~ EVENING
D7. A home of marital bliss. ~ NEST
D9. Heavy dates (abbr.). ~ HD
D10. Where cats go at night. ~ OUT
D11. A short poem. (Usually written to tailors, or landlords.) ~ ODE
D12. Something a good bartender does. ~ TENDS
D14. What people should do when they make their minds up to do something. ~ DO
D15. This is an abbreviation for something that runs between two sidewalks. (Nothing to do with pedestrians.) ~ ST
D18. Enemies of the Russian navy. ~ FOES
D19. There's a lot of ginger in one of these. ~ SNAP
D21. The high muck-a-muck of Russia. (Obsolete since the Revolution.) ~ TSAR
D24. A musical instrument. (Dumb Dora thinks this is a kind of a tramp.) ~ OBOE
D26. To record in particulars. ~ ITEMIZE
D27. A triton. (Two words.) ~ SEAIDOL
D29. To call a rubber neck this would be stretching it a little. ~ ELATTIC
D30. What wives do after they make a statement to their husbands. ~ RESIATE
D32. That bucket of yore. ~ OAKEN
D33. What the Romans used to do with some of the candidates for the Senate. ~ ELECT
D35. A feminine stunt in facial artistry. ~ DAB
D36. To do this 'tis said is only human. ~ ERR
D37. A nine by twelve girl is one you feed at nine and by twelve they want to do this. ~ EAT
D39. These are wise. (Super-super simplified.) ~ YYY
D45. This comes down in the winter. (Might be most anything but rent.) ~ SNOW
D47. The first thing the auditors did when the bank cashier took home some samples. ~ AUDITED
D48. What all up-to-date murderers try and prove they are not. ~ SANE
D50. A long time. ~ EVER
D52. The king of swat. ~ BABE
D53. None but this kind of man deserves the fair; and none but this kind can live with most of them. ~ BRAVE
D55. Cupid's deadly missiles. ~ DARTS
D57. What go-getters get if they live long enough. ~ AGED
D58. Brown derbies. ~ LIDS
D61. A pig's boudoir. (Boudoir do they go when they're hungry?) ~ PEN
D62. Before. ~ ERE
D64. Indefinitely speaking this means just one. ~ AN
D65. What Hamlet was before it became a play. (abbr.) ~ MS
D66. Where your money never goes. ~ FAR
D67. The kind of a maid that men forget. ~ OLD
D69. The milkman's busy period (abbr.). ~ AM
D71. Therefore. ~ SO


